Package: int2MR
Type: Package
Title: Integrative Mendelian Randomization for Detecting Exposure-by-Group Interactions Using Group-Specific and Combined Summary Statistics
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Ke", "Xu", email = "kxu@nd.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Author: Ke Xu
Maintainer: Ke Xu <kxu@nd.edu>
Description: This package provides a function to run one round of int2MR estimation for both the exposure-outcome direct effect and the exposure-by-group interaction effect using rstan's sampling or optimization functions for effect estimation and Hessian-based standard errors. It offers options for using both two-sample and three-sample GWAS summary statistics.
Depends: R (>= 3.6)
Imports:
    MASS,
    rstan,
    stats
Suggests:
    knitr,
    rmarkdown
VignetteBuilder: knitr
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
LazyData: true
RoxygenNote: 7.3.2
